 "claims": {
  "Q1": "the engine against R-ode at each eps (node, cell, B, heat and work), third order where errors stand above the reference's floor; on the reference side R-ode against R-qss, order 1 in eps, measured on the uptake's relative error",
  "Q2": "the long-time state against R-eq at the true V (large, small and shared node); the small node also against the depletion quadratic; the total heat against G(start) - G(eq)",
  "Q3": "the engine against R-ode at every record, and against the Riccati form directly in the closed node; on the reference side R-ode against the fixed-c exponentials, with the depletion term stated",
  "Q4": "theta(alpha)/theta(1) = alpha at c << K_d and c = 100 K_d (R-eq at the true V, depletion term <= 1.6e-7), saturation at alpha, a relaxation rate independent of alpha; the kinetic (K) and affinity (A) factors as negative controls",
  "Q5": "the ledger d(G_node) + d(G_site) + H - W = 0 at the reference's rounding, heat >= 0 on every record, the controls (work x (1 + 1e-6), the site free energy dropped, the heat's sign), the closed relaxation's heat, and the background guard",
  "tolerance_basis": "the protocol pins each judged tolerance from its dt study; a tolerance has power where it lies below a world's ceiling (the smallest control's deviation / 10) and above ten times the reference's floor; the honest SSPRK(3,3) stand-in shows where an honest engine lies (power.ceilings)"
 },
